he finance receivables funding agreements, the impacts of one-time cash costs related to the Lexmark Acquisition and higher pension contributions, all of which were partially offset by the timing of working capital1, lower finance receivable originations, lower payments for accrued compensation, and lower payments for restructuring.","context":"(2)Reflects primarily costs related to the sale of IT hardware, software solutions and services by the IT Solutions segment, to the Print and Other segment.","section":"Business Overview","block":619,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001770450-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-17","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001770450","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1770450/000177045026000009/xrx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e14f2890e4531e2b7b8f862a879b864f84ca273ad2c88105b1aa383d25932aa3.bin","sha256":"e14f2890e4531e2b7b8f862a879b864f84ca273ad2c88105b1aa383d25932aa3"}},{"id":"eab0d6be9a32d71d9b04938553ae6a6bd25570e641216c7f22418aaedfa062f8","quote":"As a result of the Lexmark Acquisition in 2025 as well as other acquisitions including ITsavvy Acquisition Company, Inc (ITsavvy) in 2024, we have a significant amount of Goodwill. Our Goodwill, net balance was $2.2 billion at December 31, 2025. We assess Goodwill for impairment at least annually, or more frequently on an interim basis if we believe indicators of an impairment exist. The application of an interim or the annual Goodwill impairment test begins with the identification of reporting units, which requires judgment. A reporting unit is the same as, or one level below, an operating segment. During the first quarter of 2025, the Company updated its determination of reportable segments to align with a change in how the Chief Operating Decision Maker (CODM), our Chief Executive Officer (CEO), allocates resources and assesses performance against the Company’s 